4. Column-Family Data Store Model

Example: Student activity database.

Row Key: 101

Personal Family:
Name = Rahul
Course = BCA

Activity Family:
Login = 10:00 AM
Page = Dashboard
Action = Download

Important concepts:

Row Key: Unique identifier of a row.
Column Family: Group of related columns.
Column Qualifier: Individual column inside a family.
Cell: Combination of row key, family, qualifier, timestamp, and value.
Timestamp: Time associated with a cell value.
Version: Multiple values of the same cell can be maintained using timestamps.

RDBMS difference: RDBMS normally uses a fixed schema where every row follows the table structure. HBase allows different rows to contain different columns.

5. HBase Model for University Activity Records

For billions of activity records:

Table: student_activity

Row Key:

StudentID#Timestamp

Example:

S101#202610062300

Column Families:

student
  name
  course
  semester

activity
  login
  page
  action
  device

location
