15. Importance of Careful Data Modeling

The statement is correct because NoSQL databases provide scalability and flexibility, but performance depends heavily on data modeling.

Poor partition key:

Can create uneven data distribution.
Causes overloaded nodes or hotspots.

Poor HBase row key:

Sequential keys can create RegionServer hotspots.
Poorly designed keys can reduce write performance.

Poor column families:

Too many unnecessary families can increase complexity.
Poor grouping can cause inefficient reads.

Poor replication:

Low replication can reduce fault tolerance.
Excessive replication increases storage and network cost.

Poor query patterns:

Large scans can be slow.
Queries requiring joins are unsuitable.
Filtering large datasets after retrieval wastes resources.

